course: dictionary
lesson: 5947
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: The word master has many meanings, and the context tells you which one is meant. «The dog obeyed its master» means the person who owns and controls the dog. «Master your times tables» is different: here master is a verb, and it means to learn something so well you can do it easily.
explain: Look at the words around it. «A chess master» and «a master chef» both mean someone very skilled at something, so master means expert. «The master bedroom» has nothing to do with control or skill: master here means main or most important. Ask yourself which meaning fits the sentence.
explain: Pupils often meet master in school. A «master's degree» is a university qualification taken after a first degree, and «old masters» are great painters from long ago. To check your meaning, swap it into the sentence: if "the main bedroom" still makes sense, you have the right meaning.
fact: Master can be a noun, a verb or an adjective, so its job in the sentence changes its meaning.
fact: «Master» as a verb means to learn something until you can do it very well, such as «master fractions».
fact: «Master» as a noun can mean an expert, as in «a chess master», or a person who controls others, as in «its master».
fact: «Master» as an adjective means main or most important, as in «the master copy».
fact: In history books, a master could also mean a person who owned enslaved people or employed servants.
exercise: «Many artists mastered the rules before breaking them.» What does mastered mean here? | Forgot | Broke | Owned or controlled | *Learned something so well they could do it easily
exercise: «The dog obeyed its master.» What does master mean here? | The main dog | A skilled dog trainer | A school teacher | *The person who owns and controls the dog
exercise: In «the master bedroom», what does master mean? | *Main or most important | Expert at sleeping | A university degree | A male teacher
test: «She wanted to master her fear before the test.» What does master mean here? | To own a dog | To be a school teacher | *To control a feeling | To ignore the test
test: «The chess master won every game.» What does master mean? | The most important bedroom | *A person who is very skilled at something | A male teacher | Someone who owns servants
exam: What does «master's degree» mean? | A title for a boy | A key that opens every lock | *A university qualification taken after a first degree | A servant's job
